{
  "slug": "dod-guard",
  "name": "Dod Guard",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Definition of Done as an executable barrier for Claude Code. Stops AI agents from declaring tasks done while code is still half-baked.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**, **7 agents**, **8 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `adversarial-verification` (Use when you are acting as a DoD-Guard validator subagent (completeness-auditor, test-quality-auditor, e2e-verifier, regression-hunter, adversarial-reviewer, claim-validator)), `dod-enforcement` (Use whenever you are implementing, refactoring, or fixing code in a project that has a .dod-guard.json file), `evidence-reporting` (Use when producing any DoD-Guard report — task completion reports from the orchestrator, validator envelopes from subagents, /dod:confess…), `stub-detection-patterns` (Use when scanning code for incomplete implementations across multiple languages)\n- **Agents** (7): `adversarial-reviewer` (Hostile code review focused on bugs, edge cases, security, and race conditions), `claim-validator` (Reads the orchestrator's \"task completion report\" and validates every claim against the actual code), `completeness-auditor` (Hunts stubs, TODOs, empty functions, placeholders), `e2e-verifier` (Demands proof that the user-facing behavior actually works), `final-judge` (Reads every other DoD-Guard subagent report from .dod-guard/reports/<session>/ and emits the final aggregated verdict), `regression-hunter` (Runs the full test suite and compares against the last baseline), `test-quality-auditor` (Audits the quality of tests, not their coverage)\n- **Commands** (8): `audit` (Full multi-agent audit), `checklist` (Present the project's Definition of Done checklist (from DOD.md) with the items completed this session marked off), `confess` (Force the orchestrator into paranoid self-audit mode), `init` (Initialize DoD-Guard in the current project (creates .dod-guard.json + DOD.md + .dod-guard/ dir)), `report` (Generate a human-readable markdown report of DoD state from existing .dod-guard/reports/ — no subagents, just formatting), `stubs` (Fast scan for stubs / TODOs / empty functions across the whole project), `tests` (Audit test quality (not coverage)), `verify` (Quick 5-phase deterministic verification (snapshot → stubs → tests → e2e probe → verdict))\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `SubagentStop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install dod-guard@claude-community` from `atoslins/dod-guard`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "agent": 7,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 8
  },
